The per-file entries of the 3D menu (album preview, light table, image editor, Showfoto and slide show) are the
stereo layer's menu, "3D Input Format" (Stereo::FileChoiceMenu), and its choices are kept in the layer's per-file
store, the one Dolphin, the thumbnailers and Gwenview read (ORDER 551b; Daniel, 2026-10-23: "never touch the user
file"). A picture set to Not 3D or given a packing in Dolphin or Gwenview opens that way here, the menu shows what the
store holds, and a choice made here shows there. The file is written only by the layer's "Save the correction into the
file".

The input packing, the anaglyph pair and the swap of the eyes were kept per picture area, for the session; they are
now each file's own. Nothing digiKam offered is gone: the layer's menu holds Automatic, side by side and top and
bottom in either order, the anaglyph pairs and the swap, and adds Not 3D for one file, the interleaved packings,
picture and depth and the save into the file. "Anaglyph to side by side" stays, with its notice on colour, and keeps
the pair for the file. The program's own lasting view stays as it was (Stereo, Left eye only, Right eye only, Not 3D
for every picture, with Alt+Shift+D, L, O and N); Alt+Shift+W swaps the eyes of the picture shown.

The image editor decodes its document through the layer with the file's path, so the stored choice applies to an
edited picture too. A picture shown flat is offered no swap and no save.

A file's choice follows it when it is renamed or moved: through the desktop's file jobs (Stereo::FileChoiceMoves), and
when digiKam itself renames or moves a file, moves a folder or renames an album. A copy carries nothing.

Built against libstereo-layer-dev 1.19.0.
